Rprofile.windows: the build tools first on PATH in R sessions

etc/Rcmd_environ (r-zig's lines, build.zig rcmdEnviron) puts the
build-tools group's R_HOME/bin/toolchain/usr/bin first on PATH under R
CMD, then a conda env's MSYS dir, R_HOME/../../usr/bin, or
R_CUSTOM_TOOLS_PATH when it is set. R sessions did not: unix's
etc/Renviron sets the same PATH for every R process, and R's own
installer build turns on the Rtools block of this file, but r-zig's
Windows sessions saw only the caller's PATH. install.packages() asks
Sys.which("make") before it takes its parallel make, and whether it may
compile from source; system("sh ...") and Sys.which("pkg-config") in R
code asked the caller's PATH too. The same rule in the session, with an
empty R_CUSTOM_TOOLS_PATH read as unset as Rcmd_environ's ":-" reads it.
A missing directory (no build-tools group extracted; the standalone
tree's Library/usr/bin) is harmless. The env's dir is spelled without
"..": R's own command search (run.c's expandcmd, Sys.which) rejects a
match in a PATH entry whose ".." segments shorten it by more than ten
characters (SearchPath's second call, given the first call's size plus
ten, reports that it does not fit: kappa 2026-10-21), so in a session
this entry comes before Rcmd_environ's ${R_HOME}/../../usr/bin, which
only programs that resolve ".." themselves then reach. R's disabled
Rtools block is left as it is. feat-standalone-toolchain B25, PHASE7
open point I a, amendment Am4, F2 b.

--- a/src/library/profile/Rprofile.windows
+++ b/src/library/profile/Rprofile.windows
@@ -85,3 +85,19 @@
         Sys.setenv(PATH = paste0(path, ";", Sys.getenv("PATH")))
     }
 })
+
+## r-zig: the build-tools group's usr/bin first on PATH in R sessions, as
+## etc/Rcmd_environ puts it under R CMD (feat-standalone-toolchain B25,
+## PHASE7 open point I): R's installer line above, with
+## R_HOME/bin/toolchain/usr/bin in Rtools' place, then a conda env's MSYS
+## dir (R_HOME is <env>/Library/lib/R: Library/usr/bin, m2's), so that
+## its tools answer whatever PATH has first (PHASE7 F2 b), spelled
+## without "..", which R's own command search rejects; an empty
+## R_CUSTOM_TOOLS_PATH read as unset, as Rcmd_environ's ":-" reads it. A
+## missing directory (no build-tools group) is harmless.
+local({
+    path <- Sys.getenv("R_CUSTOM_TOOLS_PATH")
+    if (!nzchar(path)) path <- paste(file.path(R.home(), "bin", "toolchain", "usr", "bin"),
+                                     file.path(dirname(dirname(R.home())), "usr", "bin"), sep = ";")
+    Sys.setenv(PATH = paste0(path, ";", Sys.getenv("PATH")))
+})
